title the refusal half of a Glow gate wall was satisfied by the runner's own exit line
prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- then pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure-Glow lane.
think The cold roster ran 75 guards in 31 minutes and answered guards_green=74 guards_red=1 tree_moved=no. The one red is declared_ceiling, REDS %295, Mind's and gated -- the same reading the last two laps took, so no new tree red opened and the standfast pointed at the ledger's own rows. Nothing was touched while it ran; git status at close held the same three entries it held at open.
think The rota advanced 4 to 0 with no hand needed: N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 3600, and 3600 mod 5 = 0. Aether, the row that hears -- why the work exists. Its fixed seat is sound/silence, and the grain strand it carries is the one this lap turned out to be about: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, so a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything.
think The lane door wanted deciding before it wanted doing. The card said "Kyri: the Glow tree moves, then FORA31," and the Glow-tree charter's remaining ask -- folding glow/gen by letter -- needs a change to how /+ resolves an import path, which is the language and so Sound's custody. FORA31 itself I read as mine on the last two laps and that reading was wrong: the six-bodies charter gives the thirty-seat constellation table to Dream, and FORA31's switchboard lives in constel/. What is mine there is Comlink's half of the seam. The card is corrected in this round rather than left to be repeated a third time.
think So the lane's own equipment got the reading instead, through the rota's ear. tools/g/glow_vane_pair_mirrors_witness.rish runs seven Glow gates and asserts .ok on all seven -- it never reads what any of them answered -- while closing on the line "every edge exact." A count over the family put that in proportion: 55 witnesses run Glow gates, 54 read the answer, and it is the only one that does not.
think Measuring the worker's real output turned one finding into two, and the second is the deeper one. od -c on a pair gate run showed seven bytes, EXIT:0 and a newline, with no answer at all; a single-face gate showed 1 then EXIT:0. Reading the generated Rye said why: glow/lower_shop_gate.rye emits bartis_pair at line 1442 and the expect it is compared against at line 1449 from the SAME format arguments, so the generated main compares the gate to a textual copy of its own body and returns 0 for every input. A gate planted with its arms swapped exits 0 exactly like the true one.
think The wider fault was in the assertion the other 54 use. The worker appends EXIT:0 to every successful run and Rishi's contains is a plain substring test, so assert over.out contains "0" is satisfied by the exit line alone. Proven rather than reasoned: an ACCEPT run of gate-caravan-caps-bound-u32.glow prints 1 then EXIT:0, and that output passes the refusal assertion. Twenty-eight refusal halves across twenty-three walls could not fail.
think The repaired form had to work in Rishi's existing grammar or it would not get used. A literal newline breaks the parser and backslash-n is not an escape, both probed. assert (over.out contains "1") == false parses, passes on 0\nEXIT:0, and bites on 1\nEXIT:0 -- exact for a 0/1 gate, since EXIT:0 carries no 1.
obs The load-bearing proof is end to end and not a description of one. A gate planted to answer 1 on BOTH sides -- a wall with no refusal at all -- passes the old form and is refused by the new one, run through the real witness on metal. Inverting both arms was the wrong plant: it trips the accept assertion first and proves nothing about the repair.
obs Two faults, two owners, and the split is the charter's rather than a preference. The eight walls of the infrastructure half -- Comlink, Mantra, the Caravan seams -- are repaired here and their witnesses are GREEN on metal. The lowering is Glow language custody and is REPORTED at silent_pair_gates=8 rather than gated, because a guard that reds on work another lane must do is a guard someone turns off. The twenty remaining walls stand in Tally, Aurora, Rishi and the Glow corpus and ride the ratchet.
obs The tree already held the right shape one arm away. .fold_sumto in the same lowering carries the comment "the folding gate speaks its accumulator; EXIT:0 + spoken answer prove it" and calls emit_argv_speaking_main. One arm speaks, its neighbour does not, and no meter compared them -- which is %303's shape again: only a guard over two sets can see what one set is missing.
obs The vacuous witness was seated onto the standing roster at tier cadence on 20260827.183635, as the Glow-tree charter's own first step, "the roster hears the language." So the tree has been running a cadence guard that cannot fail and counting it green for a day. Rostering a witness proves it is reached; it does not prove it can refuse.
obs I graded three A files C+ before catching my own error: --service N is a 0-100 reading like the other three, and I passed 5. The card's header documents the scale; the ITINERARY Standing line did not, which is where I read it. That line now says so, which costs eleven words and saves the next lap the same hour.
obs The repaired form is exact for a 0/1 gate and a strengthening for a fold speaking an arbitrary number -- it bites on 1, 10 and 15 and would pass on 20. Named in the scan header, the row, and here rather than left to be discovered, since reading the answer line alone is exact and costs a second process.
obs Two small things on the living card were repaired in passing because the lap was already in them: a duplicated meter line under the derived-spine paragraph, and the Now block restating a role swap the Seated section states in full. The card came back to 24,536 of the 24,576 it declares.
